onths, 30% over 6 months and 29% over 1 year.\n- You would pay about 5–7 vol points less than the stock has actually been moving, roughly 17–22% below realized. That favors buying.\n- The skew is mild and slightly downward, so upside strikes are marginally cheaper still.\n- Realized vol is backward-looking, and it could fall.\n\n**Policy path**\n- Futures price a policy rate of 4.50% for 2026Q4 and 2027Q1 (95.5). They imply 4.25% for 2027Q2 and Q3 (95.75) and 4.00% for 2027Q4 (96).\n- That is 50bp of cuts by end-2027.\n- Governor Ashby said on 28 October that one 25bp cut in 2027 is the base case. She also said markets \"may be getting ahead of themselves.\"\n- If she is right, the market is pricing about one extra cut. A hawkish repricing would lift rates by roughly 25bp relative to the futures path.\n- Rho for a roughly 14-month call is modest. A 25bp move changes the value by well under 1–2%, and it also moves the forward. That is small next to the vol edge.\n- The policy-path risk is therefore a mild headwind, not a thesis-breaker.\n\n**Verdict**\n- The vol discount to realized is the main support.\n- Treat the cut pricing as a small downside risk, since the market is ahead of the Authority.\n- A slightly out-of-the-money strike around 100–110% captures the lowest implied vol.\n- These calls are attractive only if you want exposure to VLTX's holdings. That depends on the valuation and earnings case, which n2 is assessing.\n- I did not have option prices, premiums or the VLTX spot, so I could not check breakevens.","ttft_ms":2817,"type":"result","duration_ms":26787,"uuid":"3ae3d818-d53a-4a5c-802e-e683c7dd4b0b","ttft_stream_ms":2653,"time_to_request_ms":624,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":36,"system_prompt":40,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":22,"input_attachments":143,"input_hooks":49,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":56,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":60,"init_frame_send":18,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":27,"message_prep":17,"model_con